      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ohio City was founded in 1818, making it one of Cleveland’s oldest neighborhoods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://case.edu/ech/articles/o/ohio-city-city-ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Its historic borders ran from Lake Erie on the north to the Cuyahoga River on the east, with Walworth Avenue marking its western edge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://case.edu/ech/articles/o/ohio-city-city-ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s Union Depot once served three railroads, a bustling hub that helped Ohio City thrive in the 19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohio_City%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ohio City houses a Carnegie Library branch, one of the original Carnegie libraries in the United States.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://case.edu/ech/articles/o/ohio-city-city-ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Known as the “Land of Builders,” Ohio City’s early residents were pioneers who shaped the area’s growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.thisiscleveland.com/neighborhoods/cleveland-neighborhoods/ohio-city",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s name, Ohio City, reflects its early ambition to be a prominent city within the state of Ohio.",
